  "name": "Present tense: regular -are, -ere, -ire verbs",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "it-IT",
  "subtitle": "Italian verbs end in -are, -ere or -ire. Take off the ending and add the one for the person: parlare → parlo, parli, parla. Some -ire verbs add -isc-: finisco, capisci. Use the present for now, for habits and for facts.",
  "briefMarks": ["-are", "-ere", "-ire", "-isc-", "-o", "-i"],
  "source": "icanspeak Italian original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "concept": {
    "qaWithTable": true,
    "flow": [
      { "text": "stem: parl-", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "ending: -o, -i, -a …", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "parlo, parli, parla" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "Lavor<span class=\"vp-verb\">o</span> in un albergo. · Prend<span class=\"vp-verb\">i</span> l'autobus? · Fin<span class=\"vp-verb\">iamo</span> alle sei.",
    "table": {
      "caption": "Present tense: the endings",
      "rows": [
        { "pron": "io", "end": "-o" },
        { "pron": "tu", "end": "-i" },
        { "pron": "lui, lei, Lei", "end": "-a / -e" },
        { "pron": "noi", "end": "-iamo" },
        { "pron": "voi", "end": "-ate / -ete / -ite" },
        { "pron": "loro", "end": "-ano / -ono" }
      ],
      "verbs": [
        { "inf": "parlare", "forms": ["parl|o", "parl|i", "parl|a", "parl|iamo", "parl|ate", "parl|ano"] },
        { "inf": "prendere", "forms": ["prend|o", "prend|i", "prend|e", "prend|iamo", "prend|ete", "prend|ono"] },
        { "inf": "dormire", "forms": ["dorm|o", "dorm|i", "dorm|e", "dorm|iamo", "dorm|ite", "dorm|ono"] },
        { "inf": "finire", "forms": ["fin|isco", "fin|isci", "fin|isce", "fin|iamo", "fin|ite", "fin|iscono"] }
      ]
    },
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Each ending shows the person, so you do not need <em>io</em> or <em>tu</em>: <em>Parlo italiano. Parli inglese?</em>",
        "tag": "The ending"
      },
      {
        "html": "<em>io</em>, <em>tu</em> and <em>noi</em> have the same ending in all three groups: <strong>-o, -i, -iamo</strong>. Only <em>lui/lei</em>, <em>voi</em> and <em>loro</em> change: <em>parla, prende, dorme</em>; <em>parlate, prendete, dormite</em>; <em>parlano, prendono, dormono</em>.",
        "tag": "Three groups"
      },
      {
        "html": "Many <strong>-ire</strong> verbs add <strong>-isc-</strong> in four forms (io, tu, lui/lei, loro): <em>finire → finisco, finisci, finisce, finiscono</em>, but <em>finiamo, finite</em>. Learn them as you meet them: <em>capire, preferire, pulire, spedire</em>.",
        "tag": "-isc-"
      },
      {
        "html": "The present is for what happens <strong>now</strong>, for <strong>habits</strong> and for <strong>facts</strong>: <em>Oggi lavoro da casa. Il lunedì mangio da mia madre. Abito a Bari.</em> It is also for plans: <em>Domani chiamo il medico.</em>",
        "tag": "When"
      },
      {
        "html": "To say “not”, put <strong>non</strong> before the verb: <em>Non parlo tedesco.</em> There is no word like <em>do</em>: <em>Lavori oggi?</em>",
        "tag": "non"
      },
      {
        "html": "Verbs in <strong>-care, -gare</strong> keep the hard sound with an <em>h</em>: <em>cerco → cerchi, cerchiamo; pago → paghi, paghiamo</em>. Verbs in <strong>-iare</strong> have one <em>i</em>: <em>mangiare → mangi, mangiamo; studiare → studi</em>.",
        "tag": "Spelling"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Io parlare italiano</em> → ✓ <em>Parlo italiano</em>. ✗ <em>Lei abito qui</em> → ✓ <em>Lei abita qui</em>. ✗ <em>finio, capo</em> → ✓ <em>finisco, capisco</em>. ✗ <em>paghi</em> written <em>pagi</em> → ✓ <em>paghi</em>. Other verbs change more: <a href=\"/present-irregular\">Key irregular verbs</a> and <a href=\"/essere-avere\">Essere and avere</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "Regular verbs to learn first",
          "head": ["-are", "-ere", "-ire"],
